{"additions":402,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPart of #148, closes #150.\n\n- A **Table-layout saved view** now renders the way it is defined:\n  - **Columns** — the view's visible fields in its order, behind a `#` column (`view_table_columns`). Built-in fields vig cannot render as a cell (`Linked pull requests`, `Sub-issues progress`, …) and names the project no longer lists are skipped; a view without `Title` still gets one.\n  - **Initial sort** — `sortByFields` picks the sort column and direction (`▴` marks descending); changing the sort column (`h` / `l` / `s`) resets to ascending. `sort_items` gained a direction (`sort_items_dir`) — empty cells stay last either way.\n  - **Grouping** — `groupByFields` renders bold group header rows (`group_rows`): single-select options in GitHub's order, values the options no longer list after them, `No <field>` last. The selection's visual row is offset by the headers above it; the pane title says `· by <field>`.\n- Selecting a Table view switches the pane to **table mode** automatically (`t` still toggles manually); Board / Roadmap views keep the kanban until #151 / #152. The seed re-applies when the shown view actually changes (including views arriving on a refresh over an old cache), and manual mode / sort choices survive a same-view refresh.\n\n## Docs / demo\n\n- Guide (en/ja): the saved-views section describes the Table rendering.\n- `tape/demo-projects.tape` reworked: the page now opens on the saved Table view (its fields as columns), then `t` shows the kanban; GIF re-recorded against the live board.\n\n## Tests\n\n`view_table_columns` (order / skips / Title injection), `sort_items_dir` (desc keeps empties last), `group_rows` (option order, unlisted values, `No <field>` last), and pane tests for mode / columns / sort seeding, `s` resetting the direction, view switching and header offsets. 362 tests green, clippy clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":6,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-04T08:54:25Z","deletions":81,"headRefName":"feat/projects-view-table","labels":[],"number":160,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMKRp_w","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe table rendering currently assumes the `Title` column is always at index 1, which breaks icon placement and group header alignment for saved Table views where `Title` is not the second column.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nImplements Projects Table rendering driven by a GitHub Project’s saved **Table** view definition, aligning vig’s table mode with the view’s visible fields, initial sort (including direction), and grouping.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Add saved-view-driven table column selection (`view_table_columns`), grouping (`group_rows`), and directional sorting (`sort_items_dir`).\n- Seed Projects pane mode/sort/grouping from the active saved view and render group header rows in the table.\n- Update docs (en/ja) and the Projects demo tape/GIF to reflect the new saved-view Table behavior.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Updates demo script to start in a saved Table view and show toggling back to kanban. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Applies saved view configuration to pane state (mode/columns/sort/grouping) and renders grouped table rows. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Introduces view-driven table columns, grouped-row bucketing, and directional sorting while keeping empties last. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/views-projects.md | Documents how saved Table views map to columns/sort/grouping in the Projects page. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/views-projects.md | Japanese documentation update for saved Table view rendering behavior. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Re-recorded demo GIF to match the updated Projects view behavior. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/projects/panes/board.rs:776**\n* The item-kind icon is currently prefixed only when `ci == 1`, which assumes the `Title` column is always the second column. In saved Table views where `Title` is not at index 1, this puts the icon in the wrong column. Gate the icon prefix on the actual `Title` column instead.\n```\n                let text = if ci == 1 {\n                    format!(\"{} {}\", item.kind().icon(), text)\n                } else {\n                    truncate_to_width(text, MAX_CELL_WIDTH)\n                };\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 6/6 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-09-04T08:57:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"f83bbd7398f528852e14439e9ff881273c74658e"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMKUc5Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-09-04T09:03:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"b35da67f7f358f0fa047eff295c7719688ae7e77"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABMKV4gQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe table renderer still hard-codes the item icon prefix to column index 1, which breaks when a saved Table view places `Title` in a different column.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 6/6 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-09-04T09:06:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"b35da67f7f358f0fa047eff295c7719688ae7e77"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-07T04:42:24Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/34084095931/job/101624727392","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-09-07T04:42:25Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-04T09:04:55Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33856445888/job/100970760490","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-09-04T09:03:35Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-04T09:04:12Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33856445200/job/100970757218","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-09-04T09:03:36Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-04T09:04:45Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33856445888/job/100970760599","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-09-04T09:03:38Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-04T09:05:02Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33856445888/j